<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41112" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-nītor</span></b> ,
			nīti, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep. n.</i>, <i>to strive</i>
			or <i>struggle against</i>, <i>to
				withstand</i>, <i>resist</i> (rare and not
			ante-Aug.; syn.: resisto, adversor, reluctor). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quoniam alter motus alteri renititur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					2, 82, 84, § 198</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">16, 42, 81,
				§ 222</span></i>; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">os (specillo),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 5, 28, 12</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum illi renitentes pactos dicerent sese,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 5,
					49</span></i>
			 Drak.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">renitentibus vobis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Curt.
					6, 3, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 32, 50, § 118</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quo renitente,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 31, 12, 15</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">31, 13, 10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
